Description: Qt/KDE client for connecting and mounting remote NBD disks
 NBDisk is a Qt 6 / KDE Frameworks 6 desktop client that connects remote
 Network Block Device (NBD) exports to local /dev/nbd devices and mounts
 the resulting volumes.
 .
 It lists every NBD device the kernel exposes, connects and disconnects
 exports with nbd-client or qemu-nbd, shows capacity and volume state,
 and mounts or unmounts volumes through udisks or configured mount points.
 LUKS-encrypted volumes can be unlocked with a passphrase remembered in
 KDE Wallet, connection profiles reconnect at login through the bundled
 background service, and an optional privileged helper avoids repeated
 polkit prompts.
